SCOPE / COLLISION AVOIDANCE (no silent drift — covenant rule 9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- New surface: no TirePressurePanel.* file existed at the output path before this prompt
  (the sibling vehicle-detail grid lives in TirePressureSection.*; the LiveTelemetry composite owns
   LiveTirePressurePanel / LTPPanel*; the dashboard owns TirePressure*Widget). To avoid ANY duplicate
   top-level symbol in the single shared app module, every public symbol here carries the unique
   `TPPanel` prefix and the view is `struct TirePressurePanel`. Verified app-wide UNIQUE — each of
   TirePressurePanel / TirePressurePanelModel / TirePressurePanelSource / InMemoryTPPanelSource /
   TPPanelProjector / TPPanelOverallStatus / TPPanelVariant / TPPanelUnit / TPPanelSnapshot /
   TPPanelStrings / TPPanelTone / TPPanelHeader / TPPanelTile is defined exactly 1x (this surface).
   No free functions are introduced (the section's `tirePressureVariant` / `convertTirePressureFromSI`
   top-level funcs are NOT redeclared — conversion is an instance method on TPPanelUnit and the band
   classifier is a static on TPPanelVariant), so there is no clash with the sibling section.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY (web -> native)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Data sources bound via the shared state-holder seam (P1/S8); no HTTP in the view:
    useTranslation          -> TPPanelStrings (P1/S10 NSLocalizedString facade, table "TirePressurePanel")
    useUnits.formatPressure -> TPPanelFormat.pressure (ports formatPressure(paToKpa(value)))
- helpers.ts ported 1:1: TIRE_PRESSURE_PA (206800/241300/310300/344700 Pa), paToKpa (/1000 finite-guard),
    convertPressureFromSI (kPa passthrough / psi÷6.894757 / bar÷100), the getColor/getBorder band ladder
    (success/warning/danger/neutral), and the allGood/anyBad summary ternary
    (All Normal / Attention Needed / Check Pressure) in the SAME precedence (all-good wins, then any-bad,
    else the soft middle; a null corner fails all-good and is never "bad" -> Check Pressure).
    DEFAULT_PRECISION.pressure=1, DEFAULT_EMPTY_DISPLAY "—".
- Tiles: web `grid grid-cols-2 gap-3` -> a fixed two-column LazyVGrid (the panel has no sm:grid-cols-4
    breakpoint, unlike the vehicle-detail section). Each tile = short code (FL/FR/RL/RR) over the
    band-colored, monospaced value `formatPressure(paToKpa(pa))` in a band-bordered card — no per-tile
    badge (the panel summarizes all four corners with ONE chip below the grid).
- Shared components mapped: @/components/ui GlassPanel -> TSGlassPanel; the page's FadeIn -> TSFadeIn;
    Skeleton -> TSSkeleton; the band colors -> the design-system status palette
    (statusSuccess/Warning/Danger) + textMuted for the unknown band; the summary chip reuses the
    Capsule + status color treatment. The web Gauge glyph -> SF Symbol "gauge.medium"; the summary
    glyphs ✓ / ✗ / ⚠ -> "checkmark.circle.fill" / "xmark.circle.fill" / "exclamationmark.triangle.fill".
- i18n keys present in P1/S10 table (.strings): the EXACT parity key from source `common.tirePressure`
    = "Tire Pressure"; plus the web-hardcoded display text localized so NO English literal lives in Swift
    (tile codes tirePanel.cornerFl/Fr/Rl/Rr, the summary tirePanel.allNormal/attention/checkPressure,
    the no-data sentence tirePanel.noData) + the native chrome (tirePanel.noValue/live/stale/offline/
    staleBanner/offlineBanner/loading/errorTitle/retry) + spoken corner names for VoiceOver.
- States rendered (no hidden surface): loading (2x2 tile skeleton + chip skeleton), empty (web no-data
    sentence over ContentUnavailableView), error (retry), content (2-col grid + summary chip);
    connection axis live/stale/offline (freshness chip + banner + one-shot auto-refresh on the stale
    transition; offline keeps the last-known cached grid and does NOT refetch).
- Accessibility: per-tile combined labels (spoken corner name + value), decorative icons hidden,
    panel-level VoiceOver summary (title + overall status + each corner); Dynamic Type via tokens;
    Reduce-Motion respected by TSFadeIn / TSSkeleton.
- Telemetry: view.opened emitted once on start() with surface slug "TirePressurePanel" (P1/S11).

